+# Final review inv-2, cluster 4 (docs-docs)
+
+Source: base 60e287aa, head 985d1eb6 (both verified as commits). Cluster: docs/verification-matrix.md only (slice 000060, +23 lines, one new section "Threads pin: v3.6.0 and the 3.1.0 to 3.6.0 contract audit").
+
+## Scope and method
+
+The change is documentation: a contract audit of herdr-threads 3.1.0 to 3.6.0, a release table, and notes on ResurrectSeat authority, op-key idempotency and the daemon floor. No Requirement baseline row is delivered by this file itself; the production behaviour (undo resurrects, held-seat rebind on Herdr restart) is traced by the src and tests clusters, so this file is judged for accuracy against the head source.
+
+## Claims checked against head
+
+- Cargo.lock resolves herdr-threads 3.6.0 and third_party/herdr-threads/Cargo.toml is version 3.6.0; the pin file holds 7c3c09082e8894ebceec9c060b769b07e359a2ad, matching the doc.
+- The real adapter builds its client with `with_level(GRAPH_SERVICE_LEVEL)` where the constant is `ServiceSessionLevel::V4` (src/threads/adapter.rs lines 62, 310).
+- The upgrade error text "herdr-threads daemon refused service_session_v4 (...); upgrade the herdr-threads daemon to >= 3.6.0" matches adapter.rs line 69 and the service_tests expectation.
+- Discovery refuses a 3.5.x daemon by the descriptor's software_version through `daemon_floor` (adapter.rs lines 221-263), as the doc says (hg-lnw.25).
+- `restore_outcome` matches `SeatAlreadyResolved` explicitly and maps the answers per the doc's split (Done, AlreadyResolved, transient ServiceBusy, StaleHostObservation, OutcomeUnknown, definitive NotFound, Unauthorized, TargetAlreadyOwned, InvalidRequest, Unsupported, InstanceMismatch).
+- The resurrect executor key format `resurrect:<clone>:<epoch>:<replace or none>:<count>` matches src/threads/effects.rs line 1812 and the tests.
+- The adapter forgets a completed journal entry after restore refusals (`forget_completed` at adapter.rs lines 379, 443, 510), consistent with the doc's retry-under-same-key statement.
+- The service_tests.rs fake daemon answers the new operation Unsupported, as the doc states for the one test-only break.
+
